RecoverAll
==========

RecoverAll is an independent project. It is not affiliated with, endorsed by or sponsored by
R-Tools Technology Inc. (R-Studio), Runtime Software (GetDataBack) or CGSecurity / Christophe Grenier
(TestDisk, PhotoRec); those names appear only to describe the kind of features RecoverAll offers.
No code from any of them is used.

Its own code
------------

The filesystem readers (NTFS, FAT, exFAT, ext2/3/4, XFS, HFS+, ISO 9660), the signature search, the
partition search, the boot-sector repairs, the virtual RAID and the file repairs are written from the
published format specifications and documentation, among them: Microsoft's FAT and exFAT specifications
and [MS-XCA] (XPRESS, LZX), the Linux kernel's ext4, XFS and md documentation, Apple's TN1150 (HFS+),
ECMA-119 and the Rock Ridge/Joliet extensions, the UEFI specification (GPT), and the file formats' own
specifications (JPEG/EXIF, PNG, ISO base media, RIFF, ZIP, PDF and the others listed by
`recoverctl formats`).

Tools it runs (not bundled)
---------------------------

* GNU ddrescue, GPL-3.0-or-later, https://www.gnu.org/software/ddrescue/ — images failing disks.
* The Sleuth Kit (fls, icat, fsstat, pstat), IPL-1.0/CPL-1.0/GPL, https://www.sleuthkit.org — the second
  engine for APFS and UFS.
* btrfs-progs, GPL-2.0 — reads and repairs Btrfs.
* util-linux (lsblk, blkid, sfdisk, losetup, partx), GPL-2.0-or-later — disks, partition tables.
* cryptsetup, GPL-2.0-or-later — unlocks LUKS and BitLocker volumes (read-only).
* mdadm, GPL-2.0-or-later — reads Linux software-RAID superblocks.
* smartmontools (smartctl), GPL-2.0-or-later — disk health.
* e2fsprogs, dosfstools, exfatprogs, ntfs-3g / ntfsprogs, xfsprogs, hfsprogs / hfsplus-tools,
  f2fs-tools, jfsutils, reiserfsprogs — check and repair filesystems.

The design system of the app (theme.py, icons.py, worker.py, jobview.py, diskmap.py and parts of
widgets.py) is shared with CloneAndRecover, DiskHealth, LinBurn, VirtConvert&Create, AquasuiteLinux and
FirmwareLab by the same author.
